    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n338" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accepto</span></b> , āvi, ātum, 1,
			v. freq. a.
		accipio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to take</i>, <i>receive</i>, <i>accept</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 2, 2, 32</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Quint. 12, 7, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 4, 6,
				5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 34, 1, 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jugum,</span>”
				<i>to submit to</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. Ital. 7, 41</span></i>
			. (But in <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 25, 64</span></i>, the correct read.
			is coeptavere; v. Sillig. a. h. l.).</div>
